    "abstract": "Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE) encodes absolute position with a rotation matrix while incorporating explicit relative position dependency in self-attention. RoPE supports flexible sequence length, decaying inter-token dependency with increasing relative distance, and can equip linear self-attention with relative position encoding. RoFormer, a Transformer with RoPE, is evaluated on long-text classification benchmarks and outperforms its alternatives.",
    "domain": "NLP",
    "key_claims": [
      "Rotating query and key pairs by angles m*theta_i makes their inner product depend only on the relative position m - n.",
      "RoPE has a long-term decay property: the bound on the attention contribution decreases with relative distance.",
      "RoPE is compatible with linear attention by rotating feature-mapped queries and keys in the numerator.",
      "RoFormer converges faster than BERT in MLM pretraining and improves on long-text tasks (CAIL2019-SCM)."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
